STRICT CODE-BLIND SUCCESSOR REVIEW — camera-readability-r2-blind-r1
Date: 2026-09-30
OVERALL STRICT VERDICT: FAIL
Camera/readability subset: FAIL (6/9 pairs; 14/54 stills with observed failure)
Full visual craft: FAIL (9/9 pairs; all 54 frames share unfinished world/HUD/material/light presentation)
54/54 actual 1920x1080 originals individually viewed; before/after SHA256 equal for every original.

BLIND SCOPE AND REUSED SESSION
Same session/reviewer as bf9; prior verdict and previously viewed bf9 pixels remain in context. Earlier unrelated village/source-fixture tasks also occurred in this session. This is an independent successor pixels review, not a fresh-context reviewer. No Fight-camera production source, diff, solver, numerical producer verdict, or author self-report consulted for this review.
Only 54 named successor original PNGs, user-provided pair/milestone bindings and requested criteria, plus five restored reference images. Archive report files were hashed for preservation, not read as successor judging input.
Exact user-provided F21#4: Fight camera keeps both actors framed without overlap for small, normal and giant bodies (catalog P2-062/P2-092 class); code-blind judge PASS on a size matrix. Additional requested whole-creature/head/feet/antler/tail visibility relative to HUD/foreground and owner FULL Palworld/Animo creature/world plus Valheim light/atmosphere craft bar.
Opened every original individually using view_image detail=original. No cropping, recolouring, transformed sheets or montage substitutes. Ten originals revisited for contacts. Pixel observations are qualitative, not solver measurements.
Successor review does not replace or revise bf9 archived seven-pair camera FAIL/all-nine craft FAIL. Both existing archived report files' before/after SHA256 match exactly; original bf9 captures and all previous artifacts were untouched.

LIMITS
- Still images only: no performance, motion smoothness, frame rate, device, earned-path, physical-movement execution, Quick execution or co-op claim.
- Native capture provenance is supplied by the user; pixels and immutable bytes were inspected, no engine execution independently performed.
- Pose self-occlusion (rear-on face, far-side limbs/tail) is disclosed and not automatically a framing failure. Small grass strands or unproven minute contacts are not invented failures. Clear foreground cover and inadequate distant detail are failures.
- No producer numerical PASS was opened or used. Review counts are reviewer-derived observations, not producer metrics.
- Five appropriate restored boards viewed; no separate literal Animo/Valheim screenshot comparison was available among those selected boards. Their requested direction was assessed using owner boards and meadow/Palworld references, not claimed as exhaustive benchmark equivalence.
- No source, engine, import, render, export, GPU, tests, Git, tracked writes, board acceptance edits, spawned sessions or external messages. Only three requested ignored output files written.
- No literal acceptance, packaging, canonical authority or implementation-cause claim. ROOT assesses these independently.

